WEBVTT

00:01:59.961 --> 00:02:01.055
(Laughter)

00:02:01.079 --> 00:02:03.237
"A uniform," she said,

00:02:03.261 --> 00:02:05.182
and asked for my measurements.

00:02:05.206 --> 00:02:06.839
My measurements.

00:02:06.863 --> 00:02:09.331
I had a vision of myself
in a fluffy anorak,

00:02:09.355 --> 00:02:11.506
looking like the Michelin Man.

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:12.855
(Laughter)

00:02:12.879 --> 00:02:16.067
By the middle of February,
I found myself in Turin,

00:02:16.091 --> 00:02:18.302
where enthusiastic crowds cheered

00:02:18.326 --> 00:02:22.393
when any of the 80 Olympic
teams was in the street.

00:02:22.417 --> 00:02:27.213
Those athletes had sacrificed everything
to compete in the games.

00:02:27.237 --> 00:02:30.827
They all deserved to win,
but there's the element of luck.